# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the hosted Linux Address Sanitizer step.
#
# Scope: the SwiftPM-generated test runner's XCTest HARNESS, not Gama code.
# Evidence (2026-08-27, PR #24 run 33048676959, Linux job): with
# detect_leaks=1 the runner reports exactly 7 indirect leaks / 432 bytes,
# every stack rooted in libXCTest.so (XCTestSuiteRun.init, XCTMain,
# XCTMainMisc) or reached only through those frames (Foundation
# URL.lastPathComponent called by XCTMain). The suites themselves are
# Swift Testing only; SwiftPM's generated entry point still runs the
# XCTest half, which allocates process-lifetime suite metadata it never
# frees before exit.
#
# This pattern matches any frame whose module or (mangled) symbol contains
# "XCTest" — i.e. the harness. Leaks purely inside Gama code do NOT touch
# XCTest frames and still fail the job, which is the point of keeping
# detect_leaks=1.
#
# Revisit when the pinned snapshot's SwiftPM drops the XCTest side of the
# generated runner; then this file should be deleted and the job must stay
# green without it.
leak:XCTest
